IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`

-- LAYER 1 -- Part 7A of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds
-- (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 (S.I. 2017/692), United Kingdom: regs 64A to 64H
-- (lines 2095-2199 of uksi-2017-692.txt).  The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter
-- script; it is not the official text, and nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT THESE REGULATIONS DO.  Part 7A is the "travel rule" for cryptoassets: when a cryptoasset
-- business sends a cryptoasset on to another business, or to or from a customer's own ("unhosted")
-- wallet, the originator's and beneficiary's details must go with it, and the receiving business
-- must check them, chase what is missing and report repeated failures to the FCA.  Reg 64H makes a
-- cryptoasset business answer the police's written requests.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER.  As in the other modules of this encoding: a function answers JUST TRUE,
-- JUST FALSE or NOTHING; NOTHING is "the Regulations do not answer on these facts" and is never
-- read as no.  A duty "must" not discharged, a flat negative, a "provided that", "if" or "where"
-- that fails, and a fixed period outside which the text says no, answer JUST FALSE; a scope limit
-- with no "only", a list that is not closed and an answer that belongs to another section answer
-- NOTHING.  Marginal readings (a), (b) and (c) are in NOTES.md.
-- A prohibition is named for the act it permits and answers JUST FALSE where it bites (ruling N2);
-- an unmet "where" on a prohibition answers NOTHING there, because JUST FALSE would say the opposite
-- of the text (marginal reading (f), fork F6).  The same paragraph is also asked in its own polarity,
-- by a twin named for the prohibition ("the prohibition ... applies"), which answers JUST FALSE for
-- an unmet "where" and JUST TRUE where the prohibition bites (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b); fork F10).
-- Amounts are pounds sterling, already converted: `Cryptoasset transfer` in the core carries the
-- sterling value of the transfer and of those linked to it.

§ `Part 7A -- Cryptoasset Transfers (regs 64A to 64H)`

DECLARE `reg 64C act of a cryptoasset business` IS ONE OF
    `reg 64C(1) ensure the cryptoasset transfer is accompanied by the information in paragraph (5)`
    `reg 64C(2) provide the information specified in paragraph (6) within three working days of the request`
    `reg 64C(4) ensure the transfer is also accompanied by the information in paragraph (6)`
    `reg 64C(9) make an inter-cryptoasset business transfer before ensuring full compliance`
    `reg 64D(1) check the information before making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary`
    `reg 64D(2)(a) request the missing information`
    `reg 64D(5) report repeated failure to the FCA`
    `reg 64E(1) check the information before further transferring the cryptoasset`
    `reg 64E(2)(a) request the missing information`
    `reg 64E(5) report repeated failure to the FCA`
    `reg 64F(a) ensure the information also accompanies the onward transfer`
    `reg 64F(b) send on the information received after the transfer`
    `reg 64G(4) make the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary without the information requested`
    `reg 64H respond fully and without delay to the request`

§§ `Regulation 64A -- Application of this Part`

-- src:2099 | (2) This Part does not apply in respect of a transfer of funds within the meaning of Article 3.9 of the funds transfer regulation.
@ref reg 64A(2) (src:2099)
GIVEN `it is a transfer of funds within the meaning of Article 3.9 of the funds transfer regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64A(2) this Part applies in respect of the transfer` MEANS
    IF `it is a transfer of funds within the meaning of Article 3.9 of the funds transfer regulation`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part does not apply in respect of a transfer of funds within the meaning of Article 3.9" (a flat negative)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of a transfer of funds within the meaning of Article 3.9" -- another transfer is outside the paragraph
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2100 | (3) This Part does not apply to a cryptoasset transfer where both the originator and the beneficiary is a cryptoasset business acting on its own behalf.
@ref reg 64A(3) (src:2100)
GIVEN `both the originator and the beneficiary is a cryptoasset business acting on its own behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64A(3) this Part applies to the cryptoasset transfer` MEANS
    IF `both the originator and the beneficiary is a cryptoasset business acting on its own behalf`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part does not apply to a cryptoasset transfer where both the originator and the beneficiary is a cryptoasset business acting on its own behalf" (a flat negative)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where both the originator and the beneficiary is a cryptoasset business acting on its own behalf" -- another transfer is outside the paragraph
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The same paragraph asked in its own polarity: does paragraph (3) exclude the transfer?  The
-- "where" is a condition of the exclusion, so an unmet "where" is JUST FALSE (ruling of 2026-11-05,
-- (b); fork F10).
@ref reg 64A(3) (src:2100)
GIVEN `both the originator and the beneficiary is a cryptoasset business acting on its own behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64A(3) paragraph (3) excludes the cryptoasset transfer from this Part` MEANS
    IF `both the originator and the beneficiary is a cryptoasset business acting on its own behalf`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where both the originator and the beneficiary is a cryptoasset business acting on its own behalf" -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Each paragraph answers on its own (ruling E1): paragraph (1) takes the answers of (2) and (3).
-- src:2098 | (1) This Part applies in respect of a cryptoasset transfer which is not excluded by paragraph (2) or (3).
@ref reg 64A(1) (src:2098)
GIVEN `the transaction is a cryptoasset transfer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of regulation 64A(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of regulation 64A(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64A(1) this Part applies in respect of the cryptoasset transfer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the transaction is a cryptoasset transfer`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This Part applies in respect of a cryptoasset transfer" -- a transaction that is not one is outside the paragraph
        NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the transaction is a cryptoasset transfer is reg 64B's answer and it has not been given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the answer of regulation 64A(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `the answer of regulation 64A(3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which is not excluded by paragraph (2) or (3)" -- it is excluded
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Regulation 64B -- Interpretation`

-- The definitions of this regulation are closed ("means"): a thing that does not meet them is not
-- the thing defined, so each answers JUST FALSE when its conditions are not met.
-- src:2103 | “batch file transfer” means a bundle of individual inter-cryptoasset business transfers from a single originator put together by a cryptoasset business of the originator for transmission to a cryptoasset business of a beneficiary or beneficiaries;
@ref reg 64B “batch file transfer” (src:2103)
GIVEN `it is a bundle of individual inter-cryptoasset business transfers from a single originator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was put together by a cryptoasset business of the originator for transmission to a cryptoasset business of a beneficiary or beneficiaries` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64B the transfer is a batch file transfer` MEANS
    IF `it is a bundle of individual inter-cryptoasset business transfers from a single originator`
       AND `it was put together by a cryptoasset business of the originator for transmission to a cryptoasset business of a beneficiary or beneficiaries`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a bundle of ... transfers" -- a closed definition
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2104 | “beneficiary” means the intended recipient of a cryptoasset from an originator;
@ref reg 64B “beneficiary” (src:2104)
GIVEN `the person is the intended recipient of a cryptoasset from an originator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64B the person is a beneficiary` MEANS
    IF `the person is the intended recipient of a cryptoasset from an originator`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means the intended recipient of a cryptoasset from an originator" -- a closed definition
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- SEAM S-13 (answering side is reg 14A(3)(a)): the meaning of "cryptoasset" is reg 14A(3)(a)'s;
-- this regulation adds a right to, or interest in, the cryptoasset.
-- src:2105 | “cryptoasset” has the meaning given in regulation 14A(3)(a) (cryptoasset exchange providers and custodian wallet providers) and includes a right to, or interest in, the cryptoasset;
@ref reg 64B “cryptoasset” (src:2105)
-- SEAM S-13 (asking)
GIVEN `reg 14A(3)(a) the thing is a cryptoasset` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a right to, or an interest in, a cryptoasset` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64B the thing is a cryptoasset` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a right to, or an interest in, a cryptoasset`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `reg 14A(3)(a) the thing is a cryptoasset`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has the meaning given in regulation 14A(3)(a) ... and includes a right to, or interest in, the cryptoasset" -- it is neither (marginal reading (g): the definition is read as closed)
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the thing is a cryptoasset under reg 14A(3)(a) is that regulation's answer and it has not been given
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:2106 | “cryptoasset business” means a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider;
@ref reg 64B “cryptoasset business” (src:2106)
GIVEN `the person is a cryptoasset exchange provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64B the person is a cryptoasset business` MEANS
    IF `the person is a cryptoasset exchange provider` OR `the person is a custodian wallet provider`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider" -- a closed definition
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2108 | “inter-cryptoasset business transfer” means a transaction carried out by two or more cryptoasset businesses which involves the making available of a cryptoasset of an originator to a beneficiary, provided that at least one of the cryptoasset businesses involved in the transaction is carrying on business in the United Kingdom in respect of the transaction (whether that is a cryptoasset business acting for the originator or a cryptoasset business acting for the beneficiary or an intermediary cryptoasset business);
@ref reg 64B “inter-cryptoasset business transfer” (src:2108)
GIVEN `it is a transaction carried out by two or more cryptoasset businesses` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involves the making available of a cryptoasset of an originator to a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at least one of the cryptoasset businesses involved is carrying on business in the United Kingdom in respect of the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64B the transaction is an inter-cryptoasset business transfer` MEANS
    IF `it is a transaction carried out by two or more cryptoasset businesses`
       AND `it involves the making available of a cryptoasset of an originator to a beneficiary`
       AND `at least one of the cryptoasset businesses involved is carrying on business in the United Kingdom in respect of the transaction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a transaction ... provided that at least one of the cryptoasset businesses involved ... is carrying on business in the United Kingdom" -- a closed definition with a proviso
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2109 | “intermediary cryptoasset business” means a cryptoasset business which, in the course of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer—
-- src:2110 | is not acting for the originator or the beneficiary; and
-- src:2111 | receives and transmits a cryptoasset on behalf of a cryptoasset business;
@ref reg 64B “intermediary cryptoasset business” (src:2109-2111)
GIVEN `the person is a cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the course of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer it is acting for the originator or the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it receives and transmits a cryptoasset on behalf of a cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64B the person is an intermediary cryptoasset business` MEANS
    IF `the person is a cryptoasset business`
       AND (NOT `in the course of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer it is acting for the originator or the beneficiary`)
       AND `it receives and transmits a cryptoasset on behalf of a cryptoasset business`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a cryptoasset business which ... is not acting for the originator or the beneficiary; and receives and transmits a cryptoasset" -- a closed definition
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2112 | “originator” means a person who owns a cryptoasset and allows a transfer of that cryptoasset;
@ref reg 64B “originator” (src:2112)
GIVEN `the person owns a cryptoasset` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person allows a transfer of that cryptoasset` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64B the person is an originator` MEANS
    IF `the person owns a cryptoasset` AND `the person allows a transfer of that cryptoasset`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a person who owns a cryptoasset and allows a transfer of that cryptoasset" -- a closed definition
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2113 | “unhosted wallet” means software or hardware that enables a person to store and transfer a cryptoasset on their own behalf, and in relation to which a private cryptographic key is administered by that person;
@ref reg 64B “unhosted wallet” (src:2113)
GIVEN `it is software or hardware that enables a person to store and transfer a cryptoasset on their own behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a private cryptographic key in relation to it is administered by that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64B the thing is an unhosted wallet` MEANS
    IF `it is software or hardware that enables a person to store and transfer a cryptoasset on their own behalf` AND `a private cryptographic key in relation to it is administered by that person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means software or hardware that enables a person to store and transfer a cryptoasset on their own behalf, and in relation to which a private cryptographic key is administered by that person" -- a closed definition
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2114 | “unhosted wallet transfer” means the transfer of a cryptoasset either—
-- src:2115 | by an originator from an unhosted wallet to the cryptoasset business of a beneficiary, or
-- src:2116 | by the cryptoasset business of the originator to the unhosted wallet of a beneficiary,
-- src:2117 | with a view to making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary;
@ref reg 64B “unhosted wallet transfer” (src:2114-2117)
GIVEN `it is the transfer of a cryptoasset by an originator from an unhosted wallet to the cryptoasset business of a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the transfer of a cryptoasset by the cryptoasset business of the originator to the unhosted wallet of a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made with a view to making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64B the transfer is an unhosted wallet transfer` MEANS
    IF (`it is the transfer of a cryptoasset by an originator from an unhosted wallet to the cryptoasset business of a beneficiary`
        OR `it is the transfer of a cryptoasset by the cryptoasset business of the originator to the unhosted wallet of a beneficiary`)
       AND `it is made with a view to making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means the transfer of a cryptoasset either (a) ... or (b) ... with a view to making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary" -- a closed definition
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- "cryptoasset transfer" means an inter-cryptoasset business transfer or an unhosted wallet
-- transfer: the answer is the two definitions' answers, and the core's `Kind of cryptoasset
-- transfer` names which of the two it is.
-- src:2107 | “cryptoasset transfer” means an inter-cryptoasset business transfer or an unhosted wallet transfer;
@ref reg 64B “cryptoasset transfer” (src:2107)
GIVEN `the answer of the definition of inter-cryptoasset business transfer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of the definition of unhosted wallet transfer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64B the transaction is a cryptoasset transfer` MEANS
    IF `the answer of the definition of inter-cryptoasset business transfer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer of the definition of unhosted wallet transfer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the answer of the definition of inter-cryptoasset business transfer` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `the answer of the definition of unhosted wallet transfer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an inter-cryptoasset business transfer or an unhosted wallet transfer" -- it is neither
         THEN JUST FALSE
         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a definition it depends on has not been answered
         ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2118 | “unique transaction identifier” means the combination of letters, numbers or symbols determined by a cryptoasset business which permits the traceability of the transaction from the originator to the beneficiary;
@ref reg 64B “unique transaction identifier” (src:2118)
GIVEN `it is a combination of letters, numbers or symbols` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is determined by a cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it permits the traceability of the transaction from the originator to the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64B the combination is a unique transaction identifier` MEANS
    IF `it is a combination of letters, numbers or symbols` AND `it is determined by a cryptoasset business` AND `it permits the traceability of the transaction from the originator to the beneficiary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means the combination of letters, numbers or symbols determined by a cryptoasset business which permits the traceability" -- a closed definition
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- "working day" means any day other than a Saturday, a Sunday, Christmas Day, Good Friday or a
-- bank holiday under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 in any part of the United
-- Kingdom.  The Act is not staged, so the bank holidays and the day of Good Friday are named
-- inputs (lists of days); the Regulations define the term for this Part only (fork F3).
-- src:2119 | “working day” means any day other than a Saturday, a Sunday, Christmas Day, Good Friday or a day which is a bank holiday under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 in any part of the United Kingdom.
@ref reg 64B “working day” (src:2119)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the Good Fridays` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the bank holidays under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 in any part of the United Kingdom` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 64B the day is a working day` MEANS
    (NOT (`is weekend` day))
    AND (NOT (DATE_DAY day EQUALS 25 AND DATE_MONTH day EQUALS 12))
    AND (NOT (elem day `the Good Fridays`))
    AND (NOT (elem day `the bank holidays under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 in any part of the United Kingdom`))

-- The nth working day after a day, counting from the day after it.  Whether the day of the
-- request itself counts is not said; it is taken not to (fork F5).
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
      `the Good Fridays` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the bank holidays under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 in any part of the United Kingdom` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 64B the nth working day after the day` MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN day
    ELSE IF `reg 64B the day is a working day` (Date ((Day day) PLUS 1)) `the Good Fridays` `the bank holidays under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 in any part of the United Kingdom`
         THEN `reg 64B the nth working day after the day` (Date ((Day day) PLUS 1)) (n MINUS 1) `the Good Fridays` `the bank holidays under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 in any part of the United Kingdom`
         ELSE `reg 64B the nth working day after the day` (Date ((Day day) PLUS 1)) n `the Good Fridays` `the bank holidays under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 in any part of the United Kingdom`

§§ `Regulation 64C -- Information accompanying an inter-cryptoasset business transfer`

-- (5): the information that must travel with every transfer.
-- src:2126 | (5) The information specified in this paragraph is—
-- src:2127 | (a) the name of the originator and the beneficiary;
-- src:2128 | (b) if the originator or beneficiary is a firm,the registered name of the originator or beneficiary (as the case may be), or if there is no registered name, the trading name;and
-- src:2129 | (c) the account number of the originator and the beneficiary, or if there is no account number, the unique transaction identifier.
@ref reg 64C(5) (src:2126-2129)
GIVEN `the names of the originator and the beneficiary are given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the originator or the beneficiary is a firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registered name is given, or if there is no registered name the trading name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the account numbers of the originator and the beneficiary are given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is no account number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the unique transaction identifier is given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64C(5) the information specified in this paragraph is provided` MEANS
    IF `the names of the originator and the beneficiary are given`
       AND ((NOT `the originator or the beneficiary is a firm`) OR `the registered name is given, or if there is no registered name the trading name`)
       AND (`the account numbers of the originator and the beneficiary are given` OR (`there is no account number` AND `the unique transaction identifier is given`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The information specified in this paragraph is (a) ... (b) ... and (c) ..." -- one item is missing
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- (6): the further information about the originator.
-- src:2130 | (6) The information specified in this paragraph is—
-- src:2131 | (a) if the originator is a firm—
-- src:2132 | (i) the customer identification number; or
-- src:2133 | (ii) the address of the originator’s registered office, or, if different, or if there is none, its principal place of business;
-- src:2134 | (b) if the originator is an individual, one of the following—
-- src:2135 | (i) the customer identification number;
-- src:2136 | (ii) the individual’s address;
-- src:2137 | (iii) the individual’s birth certificate number, passport number or national identity card number;
-- src:2138 | (iv) the individual’s date and place of birth.
@ref reg 64C(6) (src:2130-2138)
GIVEN `the originator is a firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the customer identification number is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address of the originator's registered office, or if different or if there is none its principal place of business, is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual's address is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual's birth certificate number, passport number or national identity card number is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual's date and place of birth are given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64C(6) the information specified in this paragraph is provided` MEANS
    IF `the originator is a firm`
    THEN IF `the customer identification number is given` OR `the address of the originator's registered office, or if different or if there is none its principal place of business, is given`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) if the originator is a firm -- (i) the customer identification number; or (ii) the address" -- neither is given
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the customer identification number is given`
            OR `the individual's address is given`
            OR `the individual's birth certificate number, passport number or national identity card number is given`
            OR `the individual's date and place of birth are given`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if the originator is an individual, one of the following" -- none is given
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2122 | (1) In respect of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer, the cryptoasset business of the originator must ensure that the cryptoasset transfer is accompanied by the information specified in paragraph (5).
@ref reg 64C(1) (src:2122)
GIVEN `the transfer is an inter-cryptoasset business transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cryptoasset business is the cryptoasset business of the originator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is accompanied by the information specified in paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64C(1) the cryptoasset business of the originator has ensured that the transfer is accompanied by the information specified in paragraph (5)` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the transfer is an inter-cryptoasset business transfer`) OR (NOT `the cryptoasset business is the cryptoasset business of the originator`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In respect of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer, the cryptoasset business of the originator must" -- another transfer or another business is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the transfer is accompanied by the information specified in paragraph (5)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must ensure that the cryptoasset transfer is accompanied by" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 64C(1) (src:2122)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 64C act of a cryptoasset business`
`reg 64C(1) the cryptoasset business of the originator must ensure the transfer is accompanied by the information (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    MUST `reg 64C(1) ensure the cryptoasset transfer is accompanied by the information in paragraph (5)`

-- src:2124 | (3) This paragraph applies where each of the cryptoasset businesses executing the inter-cryptoasset business transfer (including any intermediary cryptoasset business) is carrying on business in the United Kingdom in respect of the transaction.
@ref reg 64C(3) (src:2124)
GIVEN `each of the cryptoasset businesses executing the inter-cryptoasset business transfer, including any intermediary cryptoasset business, is carrying on business in the United Kingdom in respect of the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64C(3) paragraph (3) applies to the transfer` MEANS
    IF `each of the cryptoasset businesses executing the inter-cryptoasset business transfer, including any intermediary cryptoasset business, is carrying on business in the United Kingdom in respect of the transaction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This paragraph applies where each of the cryptoasset businesses ... is carrying on business in the United Kingdom" -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- (2): "within three working days of the request": the third working day after the day of the
-- request (fork F5).  Where (3) does not apply, or there is no request, the paragraph does not
-- bite: an unmet "where" or "if" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b)).
-- src:2123 | (2) Where paragraph (3) applies, if the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary makes a request for the information specified in paragraph (6), the cryptoasset business of the originator must, within three working days of the request, also provide the information specified in paragraph (6).
@ref reg 64C(2) (src:2123)
GIVEN `paragraph (3) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary made a request for the information specified in paragraph (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the request` IS A DATE
      `the day the cryptoasset business of the originator provided the information` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the Good Fridays` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the bank holidays under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 in any part of the United Kingdom` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64C(2) the cryptoasset business of the originator has provided the information specified in paragraph (6) within three working days of the request` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`paragraph (3) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) OR (NOT `the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary made a request for the information specified in paragraph (6)`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where paragraph (3) applies, if the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary makes a request" -- an unmet "where" or "if" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE
        LET `the last day` MEANS `reg 64B the nth working day after the day` `the day of the request` 3 `the Good Fridays` `the bank holidays under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 in any part of the United Kingdom`
        IN CONSIDER `the day the cryptoasset business of the originator provided the information`
           WHEN JUST provided THEN
               IF (Day provided) LESS THAN (Day `the day of the request`)
               -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the information was provided before the request and the text does not say whether that counts as "within" the period
               THEN NOTHING
               ELSE IF (Day provided) AT MOST (Day `the last day`)
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, within three working days of the request, also provide" -- provided after the third working day
                    ELSE JUST FALSE
           WHEN NOTHING THEN
               IF (Day `the day in question`) GREATER THAN (Day `the last day`)
               -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, within three working days of the request, also provide" -- the period has passed with nothing provided
               THEN JUST FALSE
               -- NOTHING-kind (silent): nothing provided yet and the period has not yet passed
               ELSE NOTHING

@ref reg 64C(2) (src:2123)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 64C act of a cryptoasset business`
`reg 64C(2) the cryptoasset business of the originator must provide the information within three working days (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    MUST `reg 64C(2) provide the information specified in paragraph (6) within three working days of the request`

-- (4): the £800 line, "equal to or exceeds".
-- src:2125 | (4) Where paragraph (3) does not apply and the transfer is equal to or exceeds the equivalent in cryptoassets of £800 in value (taken together with any other cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked), the cryptoasset business of the originator must ensure that the inter-cryptoasset business transfer is also accompanied by the information specified in paragraph (6).
@ref reg 64C(4) (src:2125)
GIVEN transfer IS A `Cryptoasset transfer`
      `paragraph (3) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is also accompanied by the information specified in paragraph (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64C(4) the cryptoasset business of the originator has ensured that the transfer is also accompanied by the information specified in paragraph (6)` MEANS
    IF (`paragraph (3) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (transfer's `value in sterling, linked transfers taken together` LESS THAN `the transfer threshold of 800 pounds sterling`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where paragraph (3) does not apply and the transfer is equal to or exceeds the equivalent in cryptoassets of £800" -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the transfer is also accompanied by the information specified in paragraph (6)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must ensure that the inter-cryptoasset business transfer is also accompanied by" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 64C(4) (src:2125)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 64C act of a cryptoasset business`
`reg 64C(4) the cryptoasset business of the originator must ensure the transfer is also accompanied by the information (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    MUST `reg 64C(4) ensure the transfer is also accompanied by the information in paragraph (6)`

-- (7): in a batch whose beneficiary's business is wholly outside the UK, (1) and (4) do not apply
-- to each individual transfer, provided (a) and (b).  A flat negative: JUST FALSE that they
-- apply.  If the proviso fails the paragraph is silent on whether they apply (they govern
-- themselves), so NOTHING.
-- src:2139 | (7) In the case of a batch file transfer where the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary is carrying on business wholly outside the United Kingdom, paragraphs (1) and (4) do not apply to each of the individual business transfers, provided that—
-- src:2140 | (a) the batch is accompanied by the information required by paragraphs (1) and (4); and
-- src:2141 | (b) each individual transfer within the batch is accompanied by the account number of the originator, or if there is no account number, the unique transaction identifier.
@ref reg 64C(7) (src:2139-2141)
GIVEN `the transfer is a batch file transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary is carrying on business wholly outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the batch is accompanied by the information required by paragraphs (1) and (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each individual transfer within the batch is accompanied by the account number of the originator, or if there is no account number, the unique transaction identifier` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64C(7) paragraphs (1) and (4) apply to each of the individual transfers in the batch` MEANS
    IF `the transfer is a batch file transfer`
       AND `the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary is carrying on business wholly outside the United Kingdom`
       AND `the batch is accompanied by the information required by paragraphs (1) and (4)`
       AND `each individual transfer within the batch is accompanied by the account number of the originator, or if there is no account number, the unique transaction identifier`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "paragraphs (1) and (4) do not apply to each of the individual business transfers, provided that (a) ... and (b) ..." (a flat negative)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a batch file transfer where the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary is carrying on business wholly outside the United Kingdom ... provided that" -- outside the case, or the proviso unmet, the paragraph does not say that (1) and (4) apply
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The same paragraph asked in its own polarity: does paragraph (7) disapply (1) and (4) for each of
-- the individual transfers?  "In the case of a batch file transfer where ... provided that": an
-- unmet case, "where" or "provided that" is JUST FALSE (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b); fork F10).
@ref reg 64C(7) (src:2139-2141)
GIVEN `the transfer is a batch file transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary is carrying on business wholly outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the batch is accompanied by the information required by paragraphs (1) and (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each individual transfer within the batch is accompanied by the account number of the originator, or if there is no account number, the unique transaction identifier` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64C(7) paragraph (7) disapplies paragraphs (1) and (4) for each of the individual transfers in the batch` MEANS
    IF `the transfer is a batch file transfer`
       AND `the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary is carrying on business wholly outside the United Kingdom`
       AND `the batch is accompanied by the information required by paragraphs (1) and (4)`
       AND `each individual transfer within the batch is accompanied by the account number of the originator, or if there is no account number, the unique transaction identifier`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a batch file transfer where the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary is carrying on business wholly outside the United Kingdom ... provided that (a) ... and (b) ..." -- the case, the "where" or the proviso is unmet (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2142 | (8) Information relating to the originator required under this regulation must have been verified by the cryptoasset business of the originator on the basis of documents or information in either case obtained from a reliable source which is independent of the person whose identity is being verified.
@ref reg 64C(8) (src:2142)
GIVEN `the information relates to the originator and is required under regulation 64C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been verified by the cryptoasset business of the originator on the basis of documents or information, in either case obtained from a reliable source which is independent of the person whose identity is being verified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64C(8) the information relating to the originator has been verified` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the information relates to the originator and is required under regulation 64C`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Information relating to the originator required under this regulation" -- other information is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it has been verified by the cryptoasset business of the originator on the basis of documents or information, in either case obtained from a reliable source which is independent of the person whose identity is being verified`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must have been verified" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2143 | (9) A cryptoasset business of an originator must not make an inter-cryptoasset business transfer before ensuring full compliance with this regulation.
@ref reg 64C(9) (src:2143)
GIVEN `it is a cryptoasset business of an originator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has ensured full compliance with regulation 64C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64C(9) the cryptoasset business of an originator may make the inter-cryptoasset business transfer` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is a cryptoasset business of an originator`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A cryptoasset business of an originator" -- another business is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it has ensured full compliance with regulation 64C`
         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the prohibition is lifted by "before ensuring full compliance", and the paragraph does not say that the business may make the transfer
         THEN NOTHING
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not make an inter-cryptoasset business transfer before ensuring full compliance with this regulation"
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The bar of reg 64C(9) asked as its own yes/no question: JUST TRUE before full compliance is
-- ensured, JUST FALSE once it is.  The answer never says that the business has complied (delegated
-- reading (d) of 2026-11-05; fork F10).
@ref reg 64C(9) (src:2143)
GIVEN `it is a cryptoasset business of an originator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has ensured full compliance with regulation 64C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64C(9) the prohibition on making the inter-cryptoasset business transfer applies` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is a cryptoasset business of an originator`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A cryptoasset business of an originator" -- another business is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it has ensured full compliance with regulation 64C`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before ensuring full compliance with this regulation" -- the bar has lifted
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref reg 64C(9) (src:2143)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 64C act of a cryptoasset business`
`reg 64C(9) the cryptoasset business of an originator shall not make the transfer before ensuring full compliance (as a prohibition)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    SHANT `reg 64C(9) make an inter-cryptoasset business transfer before ensuring full compliance`

§§ `Regulation 64D -- Missing or non-corresponding information: the cryptoasset business of a beneficiary`

-- src:2145 | (1) When a cryptoasset business of a beneficiary receives a cryptoasset as part of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer it must, before making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary, check whether—
-- src:2146 | (a) it has received the information required by regulation 64C to be provided; and
-- src:2147 | (b) the information relating to the beneficiary corresponds with information verified by it under Part 3 (customer due diligence).
@ref reg 64D(1) (src:2145-2147)
GIVEN `it is a cryptoasset business of a beneficiary and receives a cryptoasset as part of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary it checked whether it has received the information required by regulation 64C to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary it checked whether the information relating to the beneficiary corresponds with information verified by it under Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64D(1) the cryptoasset business has made both checks before making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is a cryptoasset business of a beneficiary and receives a cryptoasset as part of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a cryptoasset business of a beneficiary receives a cryptoasset as part of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer" -- "when" counts as "where" and its clause is unmet (delegated reading (c) of 2026-11-05)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `before making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary it checked whether it has received the information required by regulation 64C to be provided`
            AND `before making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary it checked whether the information relating to the beneficiary corresponds with information verified by it under Part 3`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, before making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary, check whether" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 64D(1) (src:2145)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 64C act of a cryptoasset business`
`reg 64D(1) the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary must check the information (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    MUST `reg 64D(1) check the information before making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary`

-- (2): where it becomes aware that information is missing or does not correspond.  (a) is owed
-- for missing information; (b) and (c) are duties to consider, discharged by having considered.
-- src:2148 | (2) Where the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary becomes aware that any information required by regulation 64C to be provided is missing or does not correspond with information verified by it under Part 3, the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary must—
-- src:2149 | (a) request the cryptoasset business of the originator to provide the missing information;
-- src:2150 | (b) consider whether to make enquiries as to any discrepancy between information received and information verified by it under Part 3; and
-- src:2151 | (c) consider whether—
-- src:2152 | (i) to delay making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary until the information is received or any discrepancy resolved; and
-- src:2153 | (ii) if the information is not received or discrepancy resolved within a reasonable time, to return the cryptoasset to the cryptoasset business of the originator.
@ref reg 64D(2) (src:2148-2153)
GIVEN `it is a cryptoasset business of a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has become aware that information required by regulation 64C is missing or does not correspond with information verified by it under Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `information required by regulation 64C is missing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has requested the cryptoasset business of the originator to provide the missing information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has considered whether to make enquiries as to any discrepancy between information received and information verified by it under Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has considered whether to delay making the cryptoasset available until the information is received or any discrepancy resolved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has considered whether, if the information is not received or the discrepancy resolved within a reasonable time, to return the cryptoasset to the cryptoasset business of the originator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64D(2) the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary has done what the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is a cryptoasset business of a beneficiary`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary" -- another business is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (NOT `it has become aware that information required by regulation 64C is missing or does not correspond with information verified by it under Part 3`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary becomes aware that any information ... is missing or does not correspond" -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF ((NOT `information required by regulation 64C is missing`) OR `it has requested the cryptoasset business of the originator to provide the missing information`)
                 AND `it has considered whether to make enquiries as to any discrepancy between information received and information verified by it under Part 3`
                 AND `it has considered whether to delay making the cryptoasset available until the information is received or any discrepancy resolved`
                 AND `it has considered whether, if the information is not received or the discrepancy resolved within a reasonable time, to return the cryptoasset to the cryptoasset business of the originator`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must (a) request ...; (b) consider ...; and (c) consider" (Marginal readings, (c))
              ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Is there a duty to DELAY?  The paragraph says "consider whether to delay", which is a duty to
-- consider (the function above) and not a duty to delay.  Where the "where" is unmet paragraph (2)
-- places no duty at all (JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b)); where it is met the text neither
-- requires nor excludes a delay, so NOTHING (fork F13).
@ref reg 64D(2) (src:2148-2152)
GIVEN `it is a cryptoasset business of a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has become aware that information required by regulation 64C is missing or does not correspond with information verified by it under Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64D(2)(c)(i) the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary must delay making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is a cryptoasset business of a beneficiary`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary" -- another business is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (NOT `it has become aware that information required by regulation 64C is missing or does not correspond with information verified by it under Part 3`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary becomes aware ..." -- an unmet "where": paragraph (2) places no duty on it (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
         THEN JUST FALSE
         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "consider whether to delay" is a duty to consider, and the text neither requires nor excludes a delay
         ELSE NOTHING

@ref reg 64D(2) (src:2149)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 64C act of a cryptoasset business`
`reg 64D(2)(a) the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary must request the missing information (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    MUST `reg 64D(2)(a) request the missing information`

-- SEAM S-2 (resolved by the core, PLAN.md 5.3): "have regard to" the risk assessments and to its
-- assessment of the level of risk of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation
-- financing.  The kinds of risk its assessment covered are core `Kind of risk` values.
-- src:2154 | (3) In deciding what action to take under paragraph (2)(c) the cryptoasset business must have regard to—
-- src:2155 | (a) the risk assessments carried out by the cryptoasset business under regulations 18(1) (risk assessment by relevant persons) and 18A(1) (risk assessment by relevant persons in relation to proliferation financing); and
-- src:2156 | (b) its assessment of the level of risk of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing arising from the inter-cryptoasset business transfer.
@ref reg 64D(3) (src:2154-2156)
GIVEN `the cryptoasset business has had regard to the risk assessments it carried out under regulations 18(1) and 18A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has had regard to its assessment of the level of risk arising from the inter-cryptoasset business transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kinds of risk its assessment covered` IS A LIST OF `Kind of risk`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64D(3) the cryptoasset business has had regard to the matters in this paragraph` MEANS
    IF `the cryptoasset business has had regard to the risk assessments it carried out under regulations 18(1) and 18A(1)`
       AND `it has had regard to its assessment of the level of risk arising from the inter-cryptoasset business transfer`
       AND elem `money laundering` `the kinds of risk its assessment covered`
       AND elem `terrorist financing` `the kinds of risk its assessment covered`
       AND elem `proliferation financing` `the kinds of risk its assessment covered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must have regard to" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- SEAM S-K1 (asking): factors (a) and (d) turn on the business relationship, which is reg 4's
-- answer.  The other two factors are owed whatever reg 4 says.
-- src:2157 | (4) In assessing the level of risk for the purposes of paragraph (3)(b), the cryptoasset business must take account of factors including—
-- src:2158 | (a) the purpose and nature of its business relationship with the beneficiary and of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer;
-- src:2159 | (b) the value of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer and any cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked;
-- src:2160 | (c) the frequency of cryptoasset transfers made by or to the beneficiary via the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary; and
-- src:2161 | (d) the duration of its business relationship with the beneficiary.
@ref reg 64D(4) (src:2157-2161)
-- SEAM S-K1 (asking)
GIVEN `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it has taken account of the purpose and nature of its business relationship with the beneficiary and of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken account of the value of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer and any cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken account of the frequency of cryptoasset transfers made by or to the beneficiary via the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken account of the duration of its business relationship with the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64D(4) the cryptoasset business has taken account of the factors` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it has taken account of the purpose and nature of its business relationship with the beneficiary and of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer`)
       OR (NOT `it has taken account of the value of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer and any cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked`)
       OR (NOT `it has taken account of the frequency of cryptoasset transfers made by or to the beneficiary via the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must take account of factors including" (Marginal readings, (c))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             IF `it has taken account of the duration of its business relationship with the beneficiary`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) the duration of its business relationship with the beneficiary" is owed where there is one
             ELSE JUST FALSE
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(d) the duration of its business relationship with the beneficiary" -- where there is no relationship the factor has nothing to measure
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether there is a business relationship is reg 4's answer and it has not been given
         WHEN NOTHING THEN IF `it has taken account of the duration of its business relationship with the beneficiary` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2162 | (5) The cryptoasset business of a beneficiary must report to the FCA repeated failure by a cryptoasset business to provide any information required by regulation 64C as well as any steps the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary has taken in respect of such failures.
@ref reg 64D(5) (src:2162)
GIVEN `there has been repeated failure by a cryptoasset business to provide information required by regulation 64C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has reported to the FCA the repeated failure and any steps it has taken in respect of such failures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64D(5) the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary has reported the repeated failure to the FCA` MEANS
    IF (NOT `there has been repeated failure by a cryptoasset business to provide information required by regulation 64C`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must report to the FCA repeated failure" -- without a repeated failure there is nothing to report
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it has reported to the FCA the repeated failure and any steps it has taken in respect of such failures`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must report to the FCA repeated failure ... as well as any steps" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 64D(5) (src:2162)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 64C act of a cryptoasset business`
`reg 64D(5) the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary must report the repeated failure to the FCA (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    MUST `reg 64D(5) report repeated failure to the FCA`

§§ `Regulation 64E -- Missing information: intermediaries`

-- src:2164 | (1) When an intermediary cryptoasset business receives a cryptoasset as part of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer it must, before further transferring the cryptoasset, check whether it has received the information required by regulation 64C to be provided.
@ref reg 64E(1) (src:2164)
GIVEN `it is an intermediary cryptoasset business and receives a cryptoasset as part of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before further transferring the cryptoasset it checked whether it has received the information required by regulation 64C to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64E(1) the intermediary cryptoasset business has checked the information before further transferring the cryptoasset` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is an intermediary cryptoasset business and receives a cryptoasset as part of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When an intermediary cryptoasset business receives a cryptoasset as part of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer" -- "when" counts as "where" and its clause is unmet (delegated reading (c) of 2026-11-05)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `before further transferring the cryptoasset it checked whether it has received the information required by regulation 64C to be provided`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, before further transferring the cryptoasset, check whether" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 64E(1) (src:2164)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 64C act of a cryptoasset business`
`reg 64E(1) the intermediary cryptoasset business must check the information (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    MUST `reg 64E(1) check the information before further transferring the cryptoasset`

-- src:2165 | (2) Where an intermediary cryptoasset business becomes aware that any information required by regulation 64C to be provided is missing, the intermediary cryptoasset business must—
-- src:2166 | (a) request the cryptoasset business from which it received the transfer to provide the missing information; and
-- src:2167 | (b) consider whether—
-- src:2168 | (i) to delay the onward transfer of the cryptoasset until the information is received; and
-- src:2169 | (ii) if the information is not received within a reasonable time, to return the cryptoasset to the cryptoasset business from which it was received.
@ref reg 64E(2) (src:2165-2169)
GIVEN `it is an intermediary cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has become aware that information required by regulation 64C is missing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has requested the cryptoasset business from which it received the transfer to provide the missing information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has considered whether to delay the onward transfer of the cryptoasset until the information is received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has considered whether, if the information is not received within a reasonable time, to return the cryptoasset to the cryptoasset business from which it was received` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64E(2) the intermediary cryptoasset business has done what the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is an intermediary cryptoasset business`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the intermediary cryptoasset business" -- another business is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (NOT `it has become aware that information required by regulation 64C is missing`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an intermediary cryptoasset business becomes aware that any information ... is missing" -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `it has requested the cryptoasset business from which it received the transfer to provide the missing information`
                 AND `it has considered whether to delay the onward transfer of the cryptoasset until the information is received`
                 AND `it has considered whether, if the information is not received within a reasonable time, to return the cryptoasset to the cryptoasset business from which it was received`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must (a) request ...; and (b) consider whether" (Marginal readings, (c))
              ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Is there a duty to DELAY?  As for the beneficiary's business: "consider whether to delay" is a duty
-- to consider, so a duty to delay is JUST FALSE where paragraph (2) is not engaged and NOTHING where it
-- is (fork F13).
@ref reg 64E(2) (src:2165-2168)
GIVEN `it is an intermediary cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has become aware that information required by regulation 64C is missing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64E(2)(b)(i) the intermediary cryptoasset business must delay the onward transfer of the cryptoasset` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is an intermediary cryptoasset business`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the intermediary cryptoasset business" -- another business is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (NOT `it has become aware that information required by regulation 64C is missing`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an intermediary cryptoasset business becomes aware that any information ... is missing" -- an unmet "where": paragraph (2) places no duty on it (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
         THEN JUST FALSE
         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "consider whether to delay" is a duty to consider, and the text neither requires nor excludes a delay
         ELSE NOTHING

@ref reg 64E(2) (src:2166)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 64C act of a cryptoasset business`
`reg 64E(2)(a) the intermediary cryptoasset business must request the missing information (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    MUST `reg 64E(2)(a) request the missing information`

-- src:2170 | (3) In deciding what action to take under paragraph (2)(b) an intermediary cryptoasset business must have regard to—
-- src:2171 | (a) the risk assessments carried out by the intermediary cryptoasset business under regulations 18(1) and 18A(1); and
-- src:2172 | (b) its assessment of the level of risk of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing arising from the inter-cryptoasset business transfer.
@ref reg 64E(3) (src:2170-2172)
GIVEN `the intermediary cryptoasset business has had regard to the risk assessments it carried out under regulations 18(1) and 18A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has had regard to its assessment of the level of risk arising from the inter-cryptoasset business transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kinds of risk its assessment covered` IS A LIST OF `Kind of risk`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64E(3) the intermediary cryptoasset business has had regard to the matters in this paragraph` MEANS
    IF `the intermediary cryptoasset business has had regard to the risk assessments it carried out under regulations 18(1) and 18A(1)`
       AND `it has had regard to its assessment of the level of risk arising from the inter-cryptoasset business transfer`
       AND elem `money laundering` `the kinds of risk its assessment covered`
       AND elem `terrorist financing` `the kinds of risk its assessment covered`
       AND elem `proliferation financing` `the kinds of risk its assessment covered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must have regard to" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- SEAM S-K1 (asking): factor (a) turns on the business relationship with its customer cryptoasset
-- business.
-- src:2173 | (4) In assessing the level of risk under paragraph (3)(b) the intermediary cryptoasset business must take account of factors including—
-- src:2174 | (a) the purpose and nature of the business relationship with its customer cryptoasset business, and of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer; and
-- src:2175 | (b) the value of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer and any cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked.
@ref reg 64E(4) (src:2173-2175)
-- SEAM S-K1 (asking)
GIVEN `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it has taken account of the purpose and nature of the business relationship with its customer cryptoasset business, and of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken account of the value of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer and any cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64E(4) the intermediary cryptoasset business has taken account of the factors` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it has taken account of the value of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer and any cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must take account of factors including (b) the value" (Marginal readings, (c))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `it has taken account of the purpose and nature of the business relationship with its customer cryptoasset business, and of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE CONSIDER `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship`
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) the purpose and nature of the business relationship ..., and of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer" is owed where there is a relationship
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer" is owed whether or not there is a relationship
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
              -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether there is a business relationship is reg 4's answer and it has not been given
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:2176 | (5) An intermediary cryptoasset business must report to the FCA repeated failure by a cryptoasset business to provide any information required by regulation 64C as well as any steps the intermediary cryptoasset business has taken in respect of such failures.
@ref reg 64E(5) (src:2176)
GIVEN `there has been repeated failure by a cryptoasset business to provide information required by regulation 64C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has reported to the FCA the repeated failure and any steps it has taken in respect of such failures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64E(5) the intermediary cryptoasset business has reported the repeated failure to the FCA` MEANS
    IF (NOT `there has been repeated failure by a cryptoasset business to provide information required by regulation 64C`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must report to the FCA repeated failure" -- without a repeated failure there is nothing to report
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it has reported to the FCA the repeated failure and any steps it has taken in respect of such failures`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must report to the FCA repeated failure ... as well as any steps" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 64E(5) (src:2176)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 64C act of a cryptoasset business`
`reg 64E(5) the intermediary cryptoasset business must report the repeated failure to the FCA (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    MUST `reg 64E(5) report repeated failure to the FCA`

§§ `Regulation 64F -- Retention of information with an inter-cryptoasset business transfer: intermediaries`

-- src:2178 | An intermediary cryptoasset business must—
-- src:2179 | (a) ensure that all the information that is provided in relation to an inter-cryptoasset business transfer pursuant to regulation 64C, including any that is requested to be provided before the transfer is made under regulation 64E(2)(a), also accompanies the onward transfer (whether to another intermediary cryptoasset business or to the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary); and
@ref reg 64F(a) (src:2178-2179)
GIVEN `the person is an intermediary cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the information provided in relation to the transfer pursuant to regulation 64C, including any requested before the transfer is made under regulation 64E(2)(a), also accompanies the onward transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64F(a) the intermediary cryptoasset business has ensured that all the information also accompanies the onward transfer` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is an intermediary cryptoasset business`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An intermediary cryptoasset business must" -- another business is outside the regulation
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `all the information provided in relation to the transfer pursuant to regulation 64C, including any requested before the transfer is made under regulation 64E(2)(a), also accompanies the onward transfer`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must (a) ensure that all the information ... also accompanies the onward transfer" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 64F(a) (src:2179)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 64C act of a cryptoasset business`
`reg 64F(a) the intermediary cryptoasset business must ensure the information accompanies the onward transfer (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    MUST `reg 64F(a) ensure the information also accompanies the onward transfer`

-- src:2178 | An intermediary cryptoasset business must—
-- src:2180 | (b) send on to the relevant cryptoasset business, as soon as practicable, any information requested under regulation 64E(2)(a) which is received after it has transferred the cryptoasset to the relevant cryptoasset business.
@ref reg 64F(b) (src:2178-2180)
GIVEN `the person is an intermediary cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it received information requested under regulation 64E(2)(a) after it had transferred the cryptoasset to the relevant cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sent the information on to the relevant cryptoasset business as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64F(b) the intermediary cryptoasset business has sent the information on as soon as practicable` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is an intermediary cryptoasset business`) OR (NOT `it received information requested under regulation 64E(2)(a) after it had transferred the cryptoasset to the relevant cryptoasset business`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any information requested under regulation 64E(2)(a) which is received after it has transferred the cryptoasset" -- other information is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it sent the information on to the relevant cryptoasset business as soon as practicable`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must (b) send on ... as soon as practicable" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 64F(b) (src:2180)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 64C act of a cryptoasset business`
`reg 64F(b) the intermediary cryptoasset business must send on the information received after the transfer (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    MUST `reg 64F(b) send on the information received after the transfer`

§§ `Regulation 64G -- Requesting information: unhosted wallet transfers and cryptoasset businesses`

-- (1): what a cryptoasset business may ask its customer for.  The list is not closed by "only",
-- so a request for something else is outside the permission.
-- src:2183 | (1) A cryptoasset business involved in an unhosted wallet transfer may request from its customer (whether the originator or the beneficiary)—
-- src:2184 | (a) such information specified in regulation 64C(5) as it does not already hold; and
-- src:2185 | (b) where the unhosted wallet transfer is equal to or exceeds the equivalent in cryptoassets of £800 in value (taken together with any other cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked), and where its customer is the beneficiary, the information specified in regulation 64C(6) in respect of the originator.
@ref reg 64G(1) (src:2183-2185)
GIVEN transfer IS A `Cryptoasset transfer`
      `the cryptoasset business is involved in the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information requested is information specified in regulation 64C(5) that it does not already hold` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information requested is information specified in regulation 64C(6) in respect of the originator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the customer is the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64G(1) the cryptoasset business may request the information from its customer` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the cryptoasset business is involved in the transfer`) OR (NOT (transfer's `kind of transfer` EQUALS `an unhosted wallet transfer`))
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A cryptoasset business involved in an unhosted wallet transfer" -- another business or transfer is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the information requested is information specified in regulation 64C(5) that it does not already hold`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `the information requested is information specified in regulation 64C(6) in respect of the originator`
              THEN IF `the customer is the beneficiary` AND transfer's `value in sterling, linked transfers taken together` AT LEAST `the transfer threshold of 800 pounds sterling`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) where the unhosted wallet transfer is equal to or exceeds the equivalent in cryptoassets of £800 ... and where its customer is the beneficiary" -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
                   ELSE JUST FALSE
              -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): (a) and (b) say what it may request and do not say that it may request nothing else
              ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2186 | (2) In determining under paragraph (1) whether to request information from its customer, the cryptoasset business must have regard to—
-- src:2187 | (a) the risk assessments carried out by the cryptoasset business under regulations 18(1) and 18A(1); and
-- src:2188 | (b) its assessment of the level of risk of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing arising from the unhosted wallet transfer.
@ref reg 64G(2) (src:2186-2188)
GIVEN `the cryptoasset business has had regard to the risk assessments it carried out under regulations 18(1) and 18A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has had regard to its assessment of the level of risk arising from the unhosted wallet transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kinds of risk its assessment covered` IS A LIST OF `Kind of risk`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64G(2) the cryptoasset business has had regard to the matters in this paragraph` MEANS
    IF `the cryptoasset business has had regard to the risk assessments it carried out under regulations 18(1) and 18A(1)`
       AND `it has had regard to its assessment of the level of risk arising from the unhosted wallet transfer`
       AND elem `money laundering` `the kinds of risk its assessment covered`
       AND elem `terrorist financing` `the kinds of risk its assessment covered`
       AND elem `proliferation financing` `the kinds of risk its assessment covered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must have regard to" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- SEAM S-K1 (asking): factors (a)(i) and (d) turn on the business relationship with its customer.
-- src:2189 | (3) In assessing the level of risk under paragraph (2)(b), a cryptoasset business must take account of factors including—
-- src:2190 | (a) the purpose and nature of—
-- src:2191 | (i) the business relationship with its customer (whether beneficiary or originator); and
-- src:2192 | (ii) the unhosted wallet transfer;
-- src:2193 | (b) the value of the unhosted wallet transfer and any cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked;
-- src:2194 | (c) the frequency of cryptoasset transfers made by or to the customer (whether beneficiary or originator) via the cryptoasset business; and
-- src:2195 | (d) the duration of the business relationship with its customer.
@ref reg 64G(3) (src:2189-2195)
-- SEAM S-K1 (asking)
GIVEN `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it has taken account of the purpose and nature of the unhosted wallet transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken account of the purpose and nature of the business relationship with its customer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken account of the value of the unhosted wallet transfer and any cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken account of the frequency of cryptoasset transfers made by or to the customer via the cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken account of the duration of the business relationship with its customer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64G(3) the cryptoasset business has taken account of the factors` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it has taken account of the purpose and nature of the unhosted wallet transfer`)
       OR (NOT `it has taken account of the value of the unhosted wallet transfer and any cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked`)
       OR (NOT `it has taken account of the frequency of cryptoasset transfers made by or to the customer via the cryptoasset business`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must take account of factors including" (Marginal readings, (c))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             IF `it has taken account of the purpose and nature of the business relationship with its customer` AND `it has taken account of the duration of the business relationship with its customer`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a)(i) the business relationship with its customer" and "(d) the duration of the business relationship" are owed where there is one
             ELSE JUST FALSE
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a)(i) the business relationship" and "(d) the duration of the business relationship" -- where there is no relationship these factors have nothing to measure
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether there is a business relationship is reg 4's answer and it has not been given
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             IF `it has taken account of the purpose and nature of the business relationship with its customer` AND `it has taken account of the duration of the business relationship with its customer`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING

-- (4): in the event it does not receive the information requested, it must not make the
-- cryptoasset available to the beneficiary.
-- src:2196 | (4) In the event that the cryptoasset business involved in an unhosted wallet transfer does not receive information requested under paragraph (1) it must not make the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary.
@ref reg 64G(4) (src:2196)
GIVEN `the cryptoasset business is involved in an unhosted wallet transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it requested information under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it received the information requested` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64G(4) the cryptoasset business may make the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the cryptoasset business is involved in an unhosted wallet transfer`) OR (NOT `it requested information under paragraph (1)`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the cryptoasset business involved in an unhosted wallet transfer does not receive information requested under paragraph (1)" -- no request, or another business, is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it received the information requested`
         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the prohibition is not triggered and the paragraph does not say that the business may make the cryptoasset available
         THEN NOTHING
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must not make the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary"
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The prohibition of reg 64G(4) asked in its own polarity: does it apply?  "In the event that" counts
-- as "where", so with no request, or with the information received, the event has not occurred and
-- the answer is JUST FALSE (fork F10).
@ref reg 64G(4) (src:2196)
GIVEN `the cryptoasset business is involved in an unhosted wallet transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it requested information under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it received the information requested` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64G(4) the prohibition on making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary applies` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the cryptoasset business is involved in an unhosted wallet transfer`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the cryptoasset business involved in an unhosted wallet transfer" -- another business is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (NOT `it requested information under paragraph (1)`) OR `it received the information requested`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the event that ... does not receive information requested under paragraph (1)" -- "in the event that" counts as "where" and the event has not occurred (fork F10)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref reg 64G(4) (src:2196)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 64C act of a cryptoasset business`
`reg 64G(4) the cryptoasset business shall not make the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary (as a prohibition)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    SHANT `reg 64G(4) make the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary without the information requested`

-- SEAM S-14 (answering): reg 40 asks whether the relevant person holds information or documents
-- received under reg 64C, 64D or 64G.  The fact is that it received them there and still holds them.
-- src:2122 | (1) In respect of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer, the cryptoasset business of the originator must ensure that the cryptoasset transfer is accompanied by the information specified in paragraph (5).
@ref reg 64C(1) (src:2122)
GIVEN `it received information or documents under regulation 64C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it received information or documents under regulation 64D` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it received information or documents under regulation 64G` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it holds them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 64C, 64D or 64G the relevant person holds information or documents received under that regulation` MEANS
    IF `it received information or documents under regulation 64C` OR `it received information or documents under regulation 64D` OR `it received information or documents under regulation 64G`
    THEN `it holds them`
    ELSE FALSE

§§ `Regulation 64H -- Provision of information`

-- SEAM S-15 (asking): whether the body is a law enforcement authority is reg 44(10)'s answer.
-- src:2199 | A cryptoasset business must respond fully and without delay to a request in writing from a law enforcement authority (within the meaning of regulation 44(10)) for any information held in connection with this Part which that authority reasonably requires in connection with the authority’s functions.
@ref reg 64H (src:2199)
-- SEAM S-15 (asking)
GIVEN `reg 44(10) the body is a law enforcement authority` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the request is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is held in connection with this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority reasonably requires it in connection with the authority's functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cryptoasset business has responded fully and without delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64H the cryptoasset business has responded fully and without delay to the request` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 44(10) the body is a law enforcement authority`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body is a law enforcement authority is reg 44(10)'s answer and it has not been given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a request in writing from a law enforcement authority" -- a request from another body is outside the regulation
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF (NOT `the request is in writing`) OR (NOT `the information is held in connection with this Part`) OR (NOT `the authority reasonably requires it in connection with the authority's functions`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a request in writing ... for any information held in connection with this Part which that authority reasonably requires in connection with the authority's functions" -- another request is outside the regulation
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE IF `the cryptoasset business has responded fully and without delay`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must respond fully and without delay" (Marginal readings, (c))
             ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 64H (src:2199)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 64C act of a cryptoasset business`
`reg 64H the cryptoasset business must respond fully and without delay (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    MUST `reg 64H respond fully and without delay to the request`
